        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d32fb87b-ffae-5892-84dc-c86adc0ae42b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Cecily Strong, Taran Killam, Will Forte, Sasheer Zamata, Jenny Slate, Vanessa Bayer, Nasim Pedrad, Fred Armisen, Jason Sudeikis\n- Shows/Sketches: What Up with That, Saturday Night Live\n- Roles: announcer, backup singers/dancers Pippa and Piper, Giuseppe, Vance\n\nFacts:\n- Cecily Legler Strong was born on February 8, 1984.\n- Cecily Strong is an American actress, voice actress, and comedian.\n- Cecily Strong joined Saturday Night Live in 2012 as a cast member.\n- In What Up with That, Taran Killam plays the show's announcer, a role originally played by Will Forte.\n- In What Up with That, Sasheer Zamata and Cecily Strong play the backup singers and dancers Pippa and Piper, respectively.\n- In What Up with That, Jenny Slate and later Vanessa Bayer originally preceded Sasheer Zamata in the backup singer/dancer role, and Nasim Pedrad originally preceded Cecily Strong.\n- In What Up with That, Fred Armisen plays Giuseppe, a saxophone player resembling Kenny G.\n- In What Up with That, Jason Sudeikis plays Vance, an overzealous backup dancer.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "08348b63-d583-5d7d-9f2f-fd2f6c212d6c",
        "text": "Page: What Up with That. Sentence: Supporting characters include Taran Killam as the show's announcer (originally Will Forte), Sasheer Zamata (originally Jenny Slate, later Vanessa Bayer) and Cecily Strong (originally Nasim Pedrad) as backup singers/dancers Pippa and Piper, respectively, Fred Armisen as Giuseppe, a Kenny G-like saxophone player, and Jason Sudeikis as Vance, an overzealous backup dancer.\nPage: Cecily Strong. Sentence: Cecily Legler Strong (born February 8, 1984) is an American actress, voice actress, and comedian, known as a cast member of \"Saturday Night Live\", having joined the show in 2012.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
